---
import SubpageLayout from '@layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';

const _body = `<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-hero-inner">
      <span class="section-label">Real · live · in your browser</span>
      <h1 class="t-h1">Watch a goal get planned and executed — for real.</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-sub">Pick a goal. Your browser fetches the live Traverse capability registry, builds a digest-verified snapshot, and a <strong>deterministic structural planner</strong> derives a workflow from it — matching each capability&rsquo;s declared input and output shapes, with <strong>no capability-name matching, no natural language, and no model</strong>. You review the proposed field mappings, then the <strong>local governed runtime</strong> executes the reviewed workflow in your tab and returns a redacted per-node trace. No backend, no simulation. <a href="#discover-how-its-built">How it works &darr;</a></p>
      <div class="page-hero-badges">
        <span class="badge badge-accent badge-dot">Live registry</span>
        <span class="badge">Deterministic structural planning</span>
        <span class="badge">Governed in-browser execution</span>
        <span id="discover-stats" class="badge">querying registry.traverse-framework.com…</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-sm" id="discover-root">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="t-body-sm t-muted discover-goals-intro">Each goal below is a different real goal against the live registry — from a multi-capability chain to a single target the runtime refuses to run automatically. Pick one; the terminal and graph track it end to end.</p>
    <div class="discover-goal-picker">
      <label for="discover-goal-select" class="discover-sub-h">Choose a goal</label>
      <select id="discover-goal-select" class="discover-select" aria-label="Goal"></select>
      <p id="discover-goal-blurb" class="t-body-sm t-muted discover-goal-blurb"></p>
    </div>

    <div class="discover-graph-panel card">
      <div id="discover-graph" class="discover-graph-el" data-empty="true"></div>
      <span id="discover-badge" class="discover-badge" data-state="idle">Loading…</span>
      <button id="discover-exec" class="discover-play-btn" type="button" hidden aria-label="Confirm mappings and execute for real" title="Confirm mappings and execute for real">
        <span class="discover-play-icon" aria-hidden="true">&#9654;</span><span class="discover-play-label">Execute</span>
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="discover-layout">
      <div class="terminal discover-terminal">
        <div class="terminal-header">
          <div class="code-dots"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <span class="terminal-title">goal → discover → plan → review → execute</span>
        </div>
        <div class="terminal-body discover-log" id="discover-log"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="discover-result" id="discover-result" data-outcome="idle" hidden>
        <div class="discover-result-header">
          <div>
            <div class="discover-sub-h">Goal</div>
            <div class="discover-goal-name" id="discover-plan-target">&mdash;</div>
          </div>
          <div class="discover-result-status" id="discover-result-status" data-state="idle">Idle</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="discover-sub-h">Proposed field mappings — unconfirmed until you execute</div>
          <ul class="discover-mappings" id="discover-plan-mappings"></ul>
        </div>
        <div id="discover-trace"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-sm" id="discover-generate-section" style="border-top:1px solid var(--border)">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-label">New this release &mdash; Decision 95</div>
      <h2>Real, governed text generation. No daemon, no server, no network call.</h2>
      <p class="t-body-sm t-muted">Every goal above plans against the live registry. This panel is different: it runs the exact, checked-in conformance fixture (<code>fixture.responder@1.0.0</code>) that proves the Spec 045/138 bridge described in <a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/blob/main/docs/decision-log.md">Decision 95</a> &mdash; the same governed, offline, digest-verified <code>model.execute</code> pipeline a full generative model would run through, satisfying <code>traverse.inference.generate</code> without an Ollama daemon or any network call. The fixture is small and deterministic on purpose: it scans your prompt for the letters &ldquo;hi&rdquo; and returns one of two fixed responses, so you can read the entire guest module yourself &mdash; <strong>it is not a trained language model</strong>.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="discover-gen-panel card">
      <label for="discover-gen-prompt" class="discover-sub-h">Prompt</label>
      <div class="discover-gen-row">
        <input id="discover-gen-prompt" class="discover-gen-input" type="text" value="hi there, how are you?" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" />
        <button id="discover-gen-run" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" type="button">Run &mdash; offline, in this tab</button>
      </div>
      <div class="terminal discover-terminal discover-gen-terminal">
        <div class="terminal-header">
          <div class="code-dots"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
          <span class="terminal-title">prompt &rarr; digest-verify &rarr; stage &rarr; execute (wasm-cpu)</span>
        </div>
        <div class="terminal-body discover-log" id="discover-gen-log"></div>
      </div>
      <div id="discover-gen-output" class="discover-gen-output" hidden>
        <div class="discover-sub-h">Response &mdash; genuinely computed from your prompt bytes</div>
        <p class="discover-gen-response" id="discover-gen-response"></p>
        <div class="discover-sub-h">Spec 138 <code>model.execute</code> evidence</div>
        <pre class="discover-gen-evidence" id="discover-gen-evidence"></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section-sm" id="discover-how-its-built" style="background:var(--bg-elevated);border-top:1px solid var(--border);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-label">How it works</div>
      <h2>The browser proposes. The runtime decides.</h2>
      <p><strong>Your browser</strong> fetches the public <a href="https://registry.traverse-framework.com/catalog.json">catalog.json</a>, builds a canonical <strong>digest-verified snapshot</strong>, prepares the exact WASM + contracts for the capabilities in play, and runs <code>traverse-embedder-web</code>&rsquo;s browser-local planner (<a href="https://github.com/traverse-framework/traverse/blob/main/specs/1277-browser-local-workflow-composition/spec.md">Spec 1277</a>). Planning is <strong>deterministic and structural</strong>: candidates come only from Spec-113 schema-shape and declared-event relationships, bounded to a small search. It <strong>does not</strong> infer from capability names or namespaces, from natural language, from a prompt or model, or from recency — and it makes no network request after preparation.</p>
      <p><strong>Your browser does not</strong> execute anything on its own, hold runtime authority, run a language model, or talk to a Traverse backend — there is none. A proposal is an <strong>untrusted</strong> artifact with every mapping <code>unconfirmed</code>.</p>
      <p><strong>The local governed runtime</strong> takes the reviewed proposal and validates it against the immutable contracts, snapshot binding, and per-node risk class, authorizes each node (only <code>pure_read</code> / <code>deterministic</code> capabilities run here), executes them offline through a minimal WASI shim, and returns a <strong>redacted</strong> trace — per-node status and failure class only, never raw payloads. It fails closed on any drift or denial; it never fabricates a success.</p>
      <a href="/registry.html" class="btn btn-ghost btn-sm" style="margin-top:1rem">Browse the full registry &rarr;</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>`;
---
<SubpageLayout
  title={"Discover — plan and execute a goal against the live Traverse registry"}
  description={"Pick a goal; your browser discovers and deterministically plans a workflow from the live Traverse capability registry, you review it, and the governed runtime executes it in your tab. No backend, no model, no simulation."}
  canonical={"https://traverse-framework.com/discover.html"}
  crumbs={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }]}
>
  <style is:global slot="head">
    .discover-goals-intro { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; }
    .discover-goal-picker { margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
    .discover-select {
      display: block; width: 100%; font-family: inherit; font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600;
      color: var(--fg); background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius);
      padding: 0.75rem 1rem; margin-top: 0.35rem; cursor: pointer;
      appearance: none; -webkit-appearance: none;
      background-image: linear-gradient(45deg, transparent 50%, var(--fg-muted) 50%), linear-gradient(135deg, var(--fg-muted) 50%, transparent 50%);
      background-position: calc(100% - 22px) center, calc(100% - 16px) center; background-size: 6px 6px; background-repeat: no-repeat;
    }
    .discover-select:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
    .discover-goal-blurb { line-height: 1.55; margin: 0.55rem 0 0; }

    .discover-graph-panel { position: relative; padding: 0.75rem 0.75rem 3.25rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
    .discover-graph-el { width: 100%; height: 240px; }
    .discover-graph-el[data-empty="true"]::after { content: "Planning…"; position: absolute; inset: 0; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; color: var(--fg-subtle); font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.8rem; }
    .discover-badge { position: absolute; right: 1.1rem; top: 1.1rem; z-index: 5; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.7rem; padding: 0.3rem 0.6rem; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--bg-elevated); color: var(--fg-muted); }
    .discover-badge[data-state="running"] { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }
    .discover-badge[data-state="planned"] { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }
    .discover-badge[data-state="executed"] { border-color: var(--success); color: var(--success); }
    .discover-badge[data-state="failed"] { border-color: #e8907d; color: #e8907d; }
    .discover-badge[data-state="noplan"] { border-color: var(--fg-subtle); color: var(--fg-subtle); }

    .discover-play-btn {
      position: absolute; left: 50%; bottom: 0.85rem; transform: translateX(-50%); z-index: 5;
      display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.6rem 1.2rem; border-radius: 999px;
      border: 1px solid var(--accent); background: var(--accent); color: var(--bg-elevated);
      font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.85rem; cursor: pointer;
      box-shadow: 0 4px 14px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 40%, transparent);
    }
    .discover-play-btn[hidden] { display: none !important; }
    .discover-play-btn:disabled { opacity: 0.55; cursor: default; box-shadow: none; }
    .discover-play-icon { font-size: 0.7rem; }

    .discover-layout { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 1fr; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: start; }
    @media (max-width: 860px) { .discover-layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
    .discover-terminal { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
    .discover-log { min-height: 8rem; max-height: 320px; overflow-y: auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.35rem; }
    /* fixed dark editor surface in both themes — see components.css */
    .discover-log-line { font-size: 0.78rem; color: #7d99a6; white-space: pre-wrap; word-break: break-word; }
    .discover-log-line.cmd { color: #f2ecdf; }
    .discover-log-line.ok { color: #9ccdb2; }
    .discover-log-line.err { color: #e8907d; }

    .discover-result { background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); padding: 1.25rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1.15rem; }
    .discover-result-header { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; flex-wrap: wrap; padding-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .discover-goal-name { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--fg); word-break: break-all; line-height: 1.3; }
    .discover-result-status {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap;
      padding: 0.35rem 0.7rem; border-radius: var(--radius-sm); border: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--fg-muted);
    }
    .discover-result-status[data-state="running"], .discover-result-status[data-state="planned"] { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }
    .discover-result-status[data-state="executed"] { border-color: var(--success); color: var(--success); }
    .discover-result-status[data-state="failed"] { border-color: #e8907d; color: #e8907d; }
    .discover-result-status[data-state="noplan"] { border-color: var(--fg-subtle); color: var(--fg-subtle); }
    .discover-mono { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.75rem; word-break: break-all; }
    .discover-sub-h { font-size: 0.66rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--fg-subtle); margin-bottom: 0.4rem; }
    .discover-mappings { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.3rem; font-size: 0.75rem; }
    .discover-mappings code { font-size: 0.72rem; }
    .discover-unconfirmed-note { color: var(--accent); font-size: 0.72rem; line-height: 1.5; margin-bottom: 0.2rem; }
    .discover-halted-note { color: #e8907d; font-size: 0.78rem; }
    .discover-noplan { color: var(--fg-muted); line-height: 1.55; }
    .discover-cap-cards { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.4rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
    .discover-cap-card { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; text-decoration: none; padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-sm); }
    .discover-cap-id { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--fg); word-break: break-all; }
    .discover-note { font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--fg-subtle); margin: 0; line-height: 1.5; }

    .discover-gen-panel { padding: 1.25rem; }
    .discover-gen-row { display: flex; gap: 0.6rem; margin-top: 0.35rem; }
    .discover-gen-input {
      flex: 1; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--fg);
      background: var(--bg-card); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius);
      padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
    }
    .discover-gen-input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
    .discover-gen-terminal { margin-top: 1rem; }
    .discover-gen-output { margin-top: 1.15rem; padding-top: 1.15rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
    .discover-gen-response {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.95rem; font-weight: 600; color: var(--fg);
      background: var(--bg-elevated); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
      padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem; margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }
    .discover-gen-evidence {
      font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.72rem; color: var(--fg-muted); white-space: pre-wrap;
      word-break: break-word; margin: 0; background: var(--bg-elevated); border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: var(--radius-sm); padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
    }
    @media (max-width: 560px) { .discover-gen-row { flex-direction: column; } }
  </style>
  <Fragment set:html={_body} />
  <script src="https://unpkg.com/@antv/g6@5.1.1/dist/g6.min.js"></script>
  <script>
    import { initDiscover } from '../scripts/discover.js';
    import { initGenerateDemo } from '../scripts/discover-generate.js';
    initDiscover();
    initGenerateDemo();
  </script>
</SubpageLayout>
